<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Stirling Bridge</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1297">1297</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-war-of-scottish-independence">First War of Scottish Independence</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stirling">Stirling</a> Bridge was fought on 11 September 1297, when Scottish forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-wallace">William Wallace</a> and Andrew Moray destroyed an English army under the Earl of Surrey as it crossed the narrow bridge over the River Forth. The victory revived Scottish resistance to Edward I, but Edward defeated Wallace at Falkirk the following year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-stirling-bridge.jpg" alt="Battle of Stirling Bridge" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Matthew White Ridley · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Battle_of_Stirling_Bridge.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>William Wallace defeated an English army at the <b>Battle of Stirling Bridge</b> in 1297 but lost at Falkirk in 1298.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-scotland">Kingdom of Scotland · Military</a></li></ul></section>
